{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "d4f21c80-1e42-4c8a-9f31-0ab1cd2e0200"/*AudioLevel*/,
  "Description": "A level-meter tap for the audio graph.\n\nPasses the wired audio sources through unchanged and outputs their combined level as a float for reactive control — e.g. driving a [Duck] or visuals. Insert it between sources and an [AudioBus], or branch a source into it. The level is measured when the routing mixer last pulled the audio, so it trails the audible signal by about a frame.",
  "InputUis": [
